      "value": "SABR appears to stand for Server Adaptive BitRate\n\nAvpro 3.3.6 June 15",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-07-16T00:08:05.110Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "There's a fix in 3.4.1 for this issue:\n\nhttps://github.com/RenderHeads/UnityPlugin-AVProVideo/issues/2183\n\nThis is currently blocking a WIP update for VRCVideoCacher that switches YouTube playback over to use the SABR protocol.\n\nThe move to SABR is mainly to future-proof things, as YouTube keeps increasing its bot checks and the legacy streams are becoming less reliable.\n\nThere's also the possibility that YouTube could eventually remove the legacy streams entirely.\n\nIf that happens, the current playback method would stop working, making YouTube playback unavailable until a SABR-based solution is in place.\n\nUpdating AVPro to 3.4.1 would unblock that work, help keep YouTube playback working going forward, and also enable support for up to 8K YouTube playback once the VRCVideoCacher update is released.",
